3:["$","p","Fabric blinds and cellular shades offer ",{"children":"Fabric blinds and cellular shades offer excellent insulation and a soft, elegant look. They're particularly effective at reducing energy costs by creating an insulating air pocket between the window and the room."}]
4:["$","div","2",{"className":"flex flex-col items-start","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-[18px] font-semibold leading-[27px] tracking-[-0.0648px] text-navy","children":"3. Sizing and Mounting Options"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 flex flex-col gap-[23px] text-[16px] leading-[23px] text-navy","children":[["$","p","Proper sizing is crucial for both appear",{"children":"Proper sizing is crucial for both appearance and function. Inside-mount blinds fit within the window frame for a clean, built-in look, while outside-mount blinds cover the entire frame and can make windows appear larger."}],["$","p","Measure each window individually — even ",{"children":"Measure each window individually — even windows that appear identical can vary by fractions of an inch, which matters for inside mounts. Width should be measured at the top, middle, and bottom; use the narrowest measurement."}],["$","p","For depth, check that your window frame ",{"children":"For depth, check that your window frame is deep enough for an inside mount. Most blinds need at least 2-3 inches of depth. If your frames are too shallow, outside mount is the better option."}]]}]]}]
5:["$","div","3",{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 md:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","div","Real wood blinds in a traditional living room",{"className":"relative h-[240px] overflow-hidden rounded-lg md:h-[280px] xl:h-[359px]","children":["$","$L2",null,{"src":"/images/resources/knowledge-grid-1.webp","alt":"Real wood blinds in a traditional living room","fill":true,"className":"object-cover"}]}],["$","div","Faux wood blinds installed in a modern bathroom",{"className":"relative h-[240px] overflow-hidden rounded-lg md:h-[280px] xl:h-[359px]","children":["$","$L2",null,{"src":"/images/resources/knowledge-grid-2.webp","alt":"Faux wood blinds installed in a modern bathroom","fill":true,"className":"object-cover"}]}],["$","div","Cellular shades providing insulation in a bedroom",{"className":"relative h-[240px] overflow-hidden rounded-lg md:h-[280px] xl:h-[359px]","children":["$","$L2",null,{"src":"/images/resources/knowledge-grid-3.webp","alt":"Cellular shades providing insulation in a bedroom","fill":true,"className":"object-cover"}]}]]}]
6:["$","div","4",{"className":"flex flex-col items-start","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-[18px] font-semibold leading-[27px] tracking-[-0.0648px] text-navy","children":"4. Light Control and Privacy Features"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 flex flex-col gap-[23px] text-[16px] leading-[23px] text-navy","children":[["$","p","Different blind types offer varying degr",{"children":"Different blind types offer varying degrees of light control. Venetian blinds allow precise angle adjustment for filtering light throughout the day. Roller shades come in light-filtering and blackout varieties."}],["$","p","For maximum versatility, consider top-do",{"children":"For maximum versatility, consider top-down/bottom-up shades that let you adjust coverage from either direction — allowing natural light from above while maintaining privacy at eye level."}],["$","p","Layering treatments (such as sheer shade",{"children":"Layering treatments (such as sheer shades behind drapes) gives you the most flexibility, letting you shift between full light, filtered light, and complete privacy without compromising on style."}]]}]]}]
